---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Returns"
  description="Returns and exchanges on handmade bolder rings, including one-of-a-kind and made-to-order pieces."
  path="/policies/returns"
>
  <div class="container section">
    <div class="page prose">
      <h1>Returns</h1>

      <p class="draft-warning">
        <strong>Draft:</strong> wording needs Samantha’s sign-off before publishing
        (MIGRATION_PLAN §14 Q12). Stripe requires a published returns policy.
      </p>

      <p class="lede">
        Every piece is made by hand, so small variations in texture, finish and stone are part of
        the work rather than faults. Anything described as imperfect on the listing is noted
        deliberately.
      </p>

      <h2>One-of-a-kind pieces</h2>
      <p>
        If something isn’t right, contact me within 14 days of delivery and we’ll sort it out.
        Pieces must be unworn and in their original condition.
      </p>

      <h2>Made-to-order pieces</h2>
      <p>
        Made-to-order rings are cast for you specifically and can’t be restocked, so they’re final
        sale unless the piece arrives damaged or differs from its description.
      </p>

      <h2>Custom commissions</h2>
      <p>
        Commissions are non-refundable once casting has begun. We’ll agree the design together
        before anything is made.
      </p>

      <h2>Damage in transit</h2>
      <p>
        If a ring arrives damaged, email <a href="mailto:boldermade@gmail.com">boldermade@gmail.com</a>
        with photos within 7 days and I’ll make it right.
      </p>

      <h2>Repairs</h2>
      <p>I don’t offer repairs or rework of existing pieces.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .page { max-width: var(--w-prose); }
  .page h1 { margin-bottom: var(--s-4); }
  .draft-warning { padding: var(--s-4); border: 1px solid var(--c-sale); border-radius: var(--r-md); color: var(--c-sale); font-size: var(--t-sm); }
</style>
